{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death","id":1212040,"title":"Punishments besides Final Death","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T16:34:18-07:00","id":1212040,"title":"Punishments besides Final Death","content":"Any suggestions on how to punish a vampire who is defying you in a covenant? Like you are in a higher position and you warned them publicly, but they continue to defy you? Also, already did the Covenant Status thing of depriving them of their merits - I think something more severe than that.<br /> <br /> Suggestions involving fire would be even better? I looked at the Brazen Bull, but I am just not sure I can get one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","user":"mikerand","date":". 04-26-2018, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:44:36-07:00","id":1212045,"title":"","content":"The Circle of the crone could create a binding spell to keep the vampire in place. The invictus or Ordo Dracul could have some kind of hidden prison","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:50:36-07:00","id":1212051,"title":"","content":"Staking, imposition of blood bonds, divestiture of feeding grounds, and similar punitive measures are fairly straightforward methods to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:57:21-07:00","id":1212056,"title":"","content":"Here's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/15961-vampire-punishments\">a thread</a> we had on the matter.<br /> <br /> I think I recall some sort of forced servitude in Requiem or maybe Masquerade fiction. Like if you've pissed off a covenant and whoever decides punishments has decided you did so wrongly, you may have to carry out a sentence of serving them for a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:57:25-07:00","id":1212057,"title":"","content":"Two suggestions on wildly different levels:<br /> 1.) Brand them with a fire iron and tell them to show the brand some time later. Failure to do so is grounds for a worse punishment. This means they have to spend WP to make the brand permanent for the rest of their unlife, stay awake to avoid the Cleansing (something which is really taxing depending on how long the brand has to stay on), rebrand themselves if they healed it. This only works if you have enough weight in the Covenant, though. Otherwise it could backfire if the victim fails to show up and you don't have the resources to either find them or make sure they stay exiled.<br /> 2.) Stake them for an extended period of time. That could really mess up their ongoing projects if they don't get any time to prepare themselves (which you shouldn't give them) and might also ruin personal relationships such as Touchstones as the victim has to explain to people they meet regularly why they suddenly disappeared for a few months without returning texts and calls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:01:35-07:00","id":1212062,"title":"","content":"Destruction of a Touchstone could be another option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:59:18-07:00","id":1212104,"title":"","content":"They would refrain from spending vitae healing the damage from the branding until the time frame expires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T19:25:13-07:00","id":1212107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212104#post1212104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would refrain from spending vitae healing the damage from the branding until the time frame expires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's not an option if you have to show the brand again the next day/week/month. When you sleep during the day, your physical state reverts back to the state it was in when you got embraced. You'll heal all wounds, although only superficially so, you don't heal the actual damage, but you will <i>look</i> fully healed after you wake up, even when in reality you're almost completely filled up with lethal damage.<br /> <br /> As Tessie herself already said, in order to keep the brand over the course of multiple nights, the vampire must either spend a Willpower to make the brand permanent (after which the vampire can never get rid of it, it will be permanent for eternity) or the vampire can stay up all day (gaining the Lethargic condition) to make sure it doesn't heal during daysleep.<br /> <br /> Either way, the vampire will suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T19:33:48-07:00","id":1212108,"title":"","content":"Just thought of a problem with the brand and any mutilation that affects more than a finger, permanent or not: The Masquerade. How is someone whose human associates have only seen in the city for all the time they've known her going to explain a new brand appearing one day? And if you keep it somewhere most people won't see, that defeats the point. Though I guess a brand on the neck could be covered by turtlenecks and scarves while interacting with humans. And amputation of anything larger than a finger is pretty uncommon unless your vampire has been working in a factory, slaughterhouse or fancy Deli. And explaining how your hand grew back should be a real treat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T20:30:50-07:00","id":1212123,"title":"","content":"Depends on the covenant and nature of defiance. Carthians are expected to defy everything on the principle. Dragons are also expected to insult and ridicule Sanctified and Acolyte beliefs and practices. Invictus are supposed to undermine their superiors to prove their worthiness to their superiors\u2019 superiors. Acolytes and Sanctified are supposed to be contemptuous of the other\u2019s practices and beliefs. Arguing in public via verbal insult flinging at a public elysium would warrant a different response than being punched in the face and breaking your jaw at the same venue. As would doing something like disobeying a directive prohibiting associating with certain kindred or harassing a favored human publicly versus privately versus punishing them for them using a discipline on you.<br /> <br /> If you want to play around with fire, just burn off single extremities of the offender in an eye for an eye format. It will take them a few nights to heal. Thumbs are good for inconveniencing them significantly while they heal.<br /> Targetting body parts needed to effectively use key disciplines is also a good choice. Eyes are typically great targets for Dominate and Auspex users. Genitalia and face for Majesty users. Feet and Arms for Celerity, Vigor, and Protean users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 09-14-2018, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:00:52-07:00","id":1212134,"title":"","content":"Regarding the brand: Aggravated damage does scar Kindred. It is the only type of damage to do so (as per the Healing section on page 91). While Aggravated damage looks unnatural on a Vampire, the scar is left behind looking natural. So Aggravated damage could leave a permanent brand that is not healed by blood or the Cleansing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T02:04:29-07:00","id":1212182,"title":"","content":"Stake them and put them on display in Elysium, force them to be at least two steps blood bound to the aggrieved person, also maiming, branding and public humiliation by Harpies are excellent punishments too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T03:15:30-07:00","id":1212189,"title":"","content":"I know that I had a scene back in the day where a character that create political problems for the Ordo Dracul was impaled and left in complete darkness for three days before he was pulled of the spear/stake/pole. Wasn't a funny experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:26:22-07:00","id":1212218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212107#post1212107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's not an option if you have to show the brand again the next day/week/month. When you sleep during the day, your physical state reverts back to the state it was in when you got embraced. You'll heal all wounds, although only superficially so, you don't heal the actual damage, but you will <i>look</i> fully healed after you wake up, even when in reality you're almost completely filled up with lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Aggravated damage (which a firebrand would do, as opposed to simply applying super-heated metal to skin) looks like a normal scar unless willpower is spent to keep it permanently. So it will be around until the kindred gets around to actually spending vitae to heal it.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:37:48-07:00","id":1212221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212218#post1212218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. Aggravated damage (which a firebrand would do, as opposed to simply applying super-heated metal to skin) looks like a normal scar unless willpower is spent to keep it permanently. So it will be around until the kindred gets around to actually spending vitae to heal it.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, language barrier. I thought firebrand means heated metal, the thing they use to mark cattle, which imo would be lethal, not aggravated, because there is no actual fire, burning chemicals or molten metal/lava nvolved, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T05:48:36-07:00","id":1212238,"title":"","content":"Isn't their a scale that makes changes your sleeping cycle so you awake durning the day and forced to sleep durning the night, use that as punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24155-flazeo25","name":"flazeo25","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:06:19-07:00","id":1212257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212221#post1212221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, language barrier. I thought firebrand means heated metal, the thing they use to mark cattle, which imo would be lethal, not aggravated, because there is no actual fire, burning chemicals or molten metal/lava nvolved, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I said fire iron. It's the tool you use to poke around inside a fire to move around pieces of firewood and such. If you heat it up it would only deal lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: A firebrand (aside from most commonly being used to describe speakers who aim to rile up a crowd) actually is a piece of burning wood, but that's tsusasi's word, not mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-27-2018, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:22:29-07:00","id":1212291,"title":"","content":"Chain them up for some good ol'-fashioned torture. (Flaying is particularly appropriate, as are the various forms of mutilation.) Restart when they frenzy and heal. <br /> <br /> Apart from the mentioned ideas, a lot of punishment would take the form of lost or suppressed assets. Your mortal allies and touchstones? Dragged before you and abused, humiliated, mutilated, and killed (pick appropriate options). Memory abuse to the punished or their mortals is another way to do it, as is of course Blood Bonds. Forced prestation debts. Transfers of property (especially privileges and feeding rights). <br /> <br /> Basically anything that harms them shy of final death, or that demands they exercise discipline either during the punishment or afterwards, would be appropriate. The point is to illustrate that the next step is worse, up to and including final death, and that the punishers are being merciful by using the offender as an object lesson for everyone else. If they didn't care about the offender and earnestly desire their reform, then staking out for the sun would be easy to arrange....<br /> <br /> Vamps who don't get the point may just be too much trouble, and flip from &quot;problem&quot; to &quot;enemy&quot; category. The establishment knows how to deal with enemies.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:01:05-07:00","id":1212312,"title":"","content":"Take away their ghoul or blood bond their childe if they have any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:28:37-07:00","id":1212324,"title":"","content":"People have said most the things I would be able to think of, but I will say that in my mage game there is currently a vampire whose mouth is stitched and sealed by his sire for some past failing. I imagine it has something to do with spilling Crone secrets. He's gone 53 years without being able to speak, and has another 47 years on the clock. It's weird, but it's the only way he'll be forgiven, is to bear the punishment dutifully, so he's done it. Obviously not great as a PC punishment, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:43:24-07:00","id":1212331,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the ideas. I will them in mind when my character punishes the other character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:54:57-07:00","id":1212359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212324#post1212324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's gone 53 years without being able to speak, and has another 47 years on the clock. It's weird, but it's the only way he'll be forgiven, is to bear the punishment dutifully, so he's done it. Obviously not great as a PC punishment, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent example of the point: in a society with, oh, not more than 100k members (and I likely over-estimate by a lot) scattered around the world you will go through a lot of trouble to endure punishment in order to mend rifts with the powerful. Or, you'll go to war. Keep in mind that time is <i>not</i> a healer, here, and the population is engaged in murder and rape nightly--moral considerations amount to &quot;is this guy or his friends materially useful in the future&quot;?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T12:15:42-07:00","id":1212380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death#post1212040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any suggestions on how to punish a vampire who is defying you in a covenant? Like you are in a higher position and you warned them publicly, but they continue to defy you? Also, already did the Covenant Status thing of depriving them of their merits - I think something more severe than that.<br /> <br /> Suggestions involving fire would be even better? I looked at the Brazen Bull, but I am just not sure I can get one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Would depend upon the covenant, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Public crucifixion might appeal to the Lancea Sanctum. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Grounding&quot;</i> a vampire might also be an option for members of both the Invictus, or the Carthians. For those who don't know the reference, it means they lock you in a coffin and bury you (un)alive until your sentence is up.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Circle of the Crone... they're a covenant of blood mages from a grab bag of pagan religions and cults. I'm pretty sure they're not short on ways to punish their enemies that are deemed worse than final death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T21:04:42-07:00","id":1212530,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> - Yes, Lancea Sanctum. I am shying away from public crucifixion because of course that would give them a Christ-like suffering making them a martyr - if they survived, they would be admired by many in the LS. My character is Mekhet and my enemy is a Daeva - they have a much better chance of rallying friends afterwards than me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T03:30:17-07:00","id":1212584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212530#post1212530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> - Yes, Lancea Sanctum. I am shying away from public crucifixion because of course that would give them a Christ-like suffering making them a martyr - if they survived, they would be admired by many in the LS. My character is Mekhet and my enemy is a Daeva - they have a much better chance of rallying friends afterwards than me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, there was somebody in real life who was crucified <b>upside down</b> in order to avoid that very problem. I believe that's where the inverted cross iconography originated from. And since the LS believe themselves to be substitutes for Satan anyways...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T03:50:38-07:00","id":1212587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212584#post1212584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not mistaken, there was somebody in real life who was crucified <b>upside down</b> in order to avoid that very problem. I believe that's where the inverted cross iconography originated from. And since the LS believe themselves to be substitutes for Satan anyways...</div> </div> </div> </div>That was Saint Peter. Not a great improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:37:55-07:00","id":1212629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212584#post1212584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, there was somebody in real life who was crucified <b>upside down</b> in order to avoid that very problem. I believe that's where the inverted cross iconography originated from. And since the LS believe themselves to be substitutes for Satan anyways...</div> </div> </div> </div>The upside-down cross as a Satanic symbol is a recent and dreadfully shallow &quot;reading&quot; made by some of the lesser reasonable anti-Christians, I'm afraid. Original legend says St. Peter consigned himself to that fate because he saw himself unworthy to be crucified in the same manner as the Son of Man. Hence the symbol is that of humility.<br /> <br /> However... combining humility and Satanism is what the Lance would approve, so it makes a 180-degree turn and ends up being an actually plausible symbol for the Church of the Damned. Symbology is fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T09:42:53-07:00","id":1212700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212629#post1212629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However... combining humility and Satanism is what the Lance would approve, so it makes a 180-degree turn and ends up being an actually plausible symbol for the Church of the Damned. Symbology is fun!</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since they might hold to the older depiction of ha-Satan as having a function much like their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T10:29:57-07:00","id":1212717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212530#post1212530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> - Yes, Lancea Sanctum. I am shying away from public crucifixion because of course that would give them a Christ-like suffering making them a martyr - if they survived, they would be admired by many in the LS. My character is Mekhet and my enemy is a Daeva - they have a much better chance of rallying friends afterwards than me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd see Lacea et Sanctum members awarding crucifixions to wash away the sins of the subject. Besides, you can only be a martyr if you die for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:28:54-07:00","id":1212748,"title":"","content":"If you don\u00b4t want to kill them you can always exile them.<br /> <br /> If you need the characters to stay in the city you can impose over them an almost imposible quest to return.<br /> <br /> If they succed they have been punished and you have won something that you wanted without risking for it your persona and if they fail well another leech less predating the humanity and rivaling you.<br /> <br /> Also considering that your character it\u00b4s a mekhet in the Lancea Sanctum you might be forced to &quot;confess&quot; your secrets and the ones from your allies to atone your sins.That would weak the character , his allies and will give him a social stigmata becuase you cannot be trusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 04-28-2018, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T03:58:42-07:00","id":1214096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1212748#post1212748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don\u00b4t want to kill them you can always exile them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But then they become somebody else's problem. And if they find out you're the one responsible for sending them their way, you've just made a new enemy, thus further exacerbating your original problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 05-02-2018, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:10:34-07:00","id":1214098,"title":"","content":"Exiling someone doesn't make the exile someone else's problem unless they continue with doing whatever warranted the punishment, but even then at least you get rid of it from your domain.<br /> But I agree that making a new enemy is rarely good. Definitely dramatically correct, but not a particularly savvy move from the exiler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:52:12-07:00","id":1214245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214096#post1214096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then they become somebody else's problem. And if they find out you're the one responsible for sending them their way, you've just made a new enemy, thus further exacerbating your original problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? You didn't send him to another domain to cause ruckus.If that guy just decided to go to the west domain instead of the south one it was his decision.If the other elder doesnt want that filthy excuse of vampyr making problems in his territory he only has to exile him again or punish him with final death.<br /> <br /> Furthermore why should an elder or ancillae risk his resources and unlife to pick a fight with another for such small thing as an anarch wannabe? Doing that he will only be doing a favour to the exiled one and damaging both himself and the other prince in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:16:45-07:00","id":1214253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214245#post1214245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? You didn't send him to another domain to cause ruckus.If that guy just decided to go to the west domain instead of the south one it was his decision.If the other elder doesnt want that filthy excuse of vampyr making problems in his territory he only has to exile him again or punish him with final death.<br /> <br /> Furthermore why should an elder or ancillae risk his resources and unlife to pick a fight with another for such small thing as an anarch wannabe? Doing that he will only be doing a favour to the exiled one and damaging both himself and the other prince in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're still the one responsible for said exile finding their way into the other domain, thus allowing them to cause problems for whoever resides there. Even if you're not deliberately sending them there to cause problems, the people in charge may still be upset with you for not disposing of the troublemaker yourself.<br /> <br /> At best, it might be perceived as a sign of weakness, and at worse, it could be perceived as a deliberate attempt at sabotage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T12:46:46-07:00","id":1214268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214253#post1214253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still the one responsible for said exile finding their way into the other domain, thus allowing them to cause problems for whoever resides there. Even if you're not deliberately sending them there to cause problems, the people in charge may still be upset with you for not disposing of the troublemaker yourself.<br /> <br /> At best, it might be perceived as a sign of weakness, and at worse, it could be perceived as a deliberate attempt at sabotage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural beings generally have better things to do with their time than point fingers in response to another domain's problem getting shunted in their direction. Exile is &quot;they're not welcome here&quot; \u2014 nothing about that prevents the neighbors from following suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T13:03:20-07:00","id":1214277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214253#post1214253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're still the one responsible for said exile finding their way into the other domain, thus allowing them to cause problems for whoever resides there. Even if you're not deliberately sending them there to cause problems, the people in charge may still be upset with you for not disposing of the troublemaker yourself.<br /> <br /> At best, it might be perceived as a sign of weakness, and at worse, it could be perceived as a deliberate attempt at sabotage.</div> </div> </div> </div>No elder it\u00b4s responsible for the missdeeds of an exiled troublemaker who chose to go to another city and elders have better things to do than to fight about little troublemakers or making enemies for the sake of it in other domain.<br /> <br /> If they can\u00b4t deal with him when the other elder did I would say the weak are they.The sabotage thing it\u00b4s something I can\u00b4t see happening if the exiled it\u00b4s just a troublemaker guy instead of a clever and adaptative challenge who vinculates himself to you (Wich it\u00b4s pretty suicidal) and you can always deny this saying he wants revenge for the exile and your rivalry wich it\u00b4s true and easy to see.The other posibility it\u00b4s if there are a rivalry between the elders of both domains in wich case it was already your enemy so fuck them.<br /> <br /> But the true point it\u00b4s that here it\u00b4s that if the exiled is that dangerous whatever domain he is in and the cunning adversary you portrait he isn\u00b4t a troublemaker , he is an enemy and he should have been quickly executed and this isn\u00b4t the case","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 05-02-2018, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T13:05:34-07:00","id":1214280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214268#post1214268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural beings generally have better things to do with their time than point fingers in response to another domain's problem getting shunted in their direction. Exile is &quot;they're not welcome here&quot; \u2014 nothing about that prevents the neighbors from following suit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Replace &quot;generally&quot; with &quot;often&quot;. Among vampires in established domains, pointing fingers is a sporting pastime--especially if doing so makes it someone else's problem to actually deal with (i.e. the Prince and his agents). <br /> <br /> Exiling has a few big pluses and minuses:<br /> <br /> 1. It permits you to appear merciful, even if you're actually taking the banished person's stuff in the process! If you're &quot;forced&quot; as a leader (thanks harpies!) to punish someone you don't really want to, then exile is a least-worst option compared to many.<br /> 2. It theoretically enables the banished to return eventually, under conditions set by you--probably to your direct benefit, but at least &quot;later&quot; in some measurable way.<br /> 3. Your problem literally goes away.<br /> <br /> A. The banished becomes someone else's problem. They may not thank you for it. Or they may: if you spin things right, the exile may work out for everyone involved and you end up with more favors! (Turning a minus into a plus.)<br /> B. The banished are still capable of stirring up trouble remotely for you, and if they do so may be out of reach of immediate retribution (which, of course, weakens your position!). They also may be able to continue tapping allies or resources in their original territory, which all at least makes things more uncertain for you.<br /> <br /> All in all, exile is superb as a punishment for people you don't really want to damage, but have to get away for a while until the gossip burns out. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T14:47:47-07:00","id":1214326,"title":"","content":"People are making exiling into a bigger deal than it is. It worked historically. No reason it wouldn't work here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T14:58:14-07:00","id":1214329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214280#post1214280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Replace &quot;generally&quot; with &quot;often&quot;. Among vampires in established domains, pointing fingers is a sporting pastime--especially if doing so makes it someone else's problem to actually deal with (i.e. the Prince and his agents).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because my meaning was apparently unclear:<br /> <br /> Organized supernaturals generally have better things to do with their time than <i>pick an argument with an entire different city for the sake of dealing with a hobo that wandered into the wrong neighborhood</i>. The Prince may find another domain's exile becoming a point of politics, but <i>the specific angle of &quot;force the folks that exiled them to take them back&quot;</i> is more trouble than most monsters with local concerns are going to bother with when &quot;exile them yourselves&quot; is on the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T17:40:40-07:00","id":1214370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1212040-punishments-besides-final-death?p=1214253#post1214253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're still the one responsible for said exile finding their way into the other domain, thus allowing them to cause problems for whoever resides there. Even if you're not deliberately sending them there to cause problems, the people in charge may still be upset with you for not disposing of the troublemaker yourself.<br /> <br /> At best, it might be perceived as a sign of weakness, and at worse, it could be perceived as a deliberate attempt at sabotage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your premise hinges upon the fact that the next domain over will accept the exile in the first place. If, for instance, some high up Invictus member in Chicago is on speaking terms with their Dragon ex-girlfriend in Minneapolis and fills them in on the exile's antics, that same Dragon may decide to suggest that it's not in Minneapolis' best interests to allow the exile to settle there either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T07:52:30-07:00","id":1215056,"title":"","content":"are punishments involving pain invalidated by the ability to regerate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://